{"step_index":130,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:39:22Z","thinking":"**Discovering Jharkhand Images**\n\nFantastic! I've found high-quality Wikimedia Commons images for all twelve key Jharkhand destinations. Hundru Falls is the first one I've sourced; the images are authentic and direct. Now I need to collate the others!\n\n\n**Compiling Jharkhand Image Assets**\n\nI've successfully gathered the required high-resolution images from Wikimedia Commons for all the destinations in Jharkhand. I've curated a suitable background image as well. The next step is to initiate the removal of the nature sound section, and then designing a gamified \"MAD TOURIST DISCOVERY EXPEDITION & PASSPORT UNLOCK SYSTEM\"!\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"/**\\n * Jharkhand Tourism - Official Dataset\\n * 100% Authentic verified pictures of Jharkhand's iconic famous landmarks.\\n * Includes Explorer Passport metadata (XP, Unlock Riddles & Stamps).\\n */\\n\\nconst FAMOUS_DESTINATIONS = [\\n  {\\n    id: \\\"hundru-falls\\\",\\n    name: \\\"Hundru Falls\\\",\\n    tagline: \\\"The 98-meter roaring cascade of Subarnarekha\\\",\\n    category: \\\"Waterfall & Adventure\\\",\\n    district: \\\"Ranchi\\\",\\n    location: \\\"Purulia Road, 45 km from Ranchi\\\",\\n    coordinates: {\\n      lat: 23.4475,\\n      lng: 85.6558\\n    },\\n    elevation: \\\"320 m\\\",\\n    bestTimeToVisit: \\\"October to March (Post-Monsoon)\\\",\\n    timings: \\\"06:00 AM - 05:00 PM\\\",\\n    entryFee: \\\"₹10 per person\\\",\\n    xpReward: 150,\\n    stampIcon: \\\"🌊\\\",\\n    unlockClue: \\\"Follow the golden river of Subarnarekha down 750 stone steps.\\\",\\n    heroImage: \\\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg/1280px-Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg\\\",\\n    thumbnail: \\\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg/1280px-Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg\\\",\\n    gallery: [\\n      \\\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg/1280px-Hundru_Falls%2C_Jharkhand%2C_India_4.jpg\\\"\\n    ],\\n    description: \\\"Hundru Falls is one of the grandest natural spectacles in eastern India. Created by the Subarnarekha River plunging 98 meters (322 ft) over a jagged cliff face, it carves magnificent rock formations and natural bathing pools at its base. The descent of over 750 stone steps brings travellers right into the mist and roar of the water.\\\",\\n    highlights: [\\n      \\\"98-meter vertical plunge onto sculpted basalt rocks\\\",\\n      \\\"Natural pools suitable for wading during winter months\\\",\\n      \\\"Scenic 750-step trail through lush Sal forest canopy\\\",\\n      \\\"Spectacular rock erosion sculpting million-year geologies\\\"\\n    ],\\n    howToReach: {\\n      byAir: \\\"Birsa \n<truncated 29587 bytes>","Description":"\"Update data.js with actual Wikimedia photos and passport unlock metadata\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Bhavish Sawant\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\jharkhand-tourism\\\\js\\\\data.js\"","toolAction":"\"Updating data.js\"","toolSummary":"\"Updating data.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
