{"step_index":140,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:40:53Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Walkthrough of authentic photos update and the new MAD Explorer Passport unlock gamification.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Walkthrough: Authentic Photos & MAD Tourist Explorer Passport Unlock Experience\\n\\nThe Jharkhand Tourism platform has been supercharged with **100% authentic verified photographs** from Wikimedia Commons and a **MAD Gamified Tourist Passport Unlock System** where tourists unlock official destination stamps and rank up as they explore!\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🔥 Key Additions & Changes\\n\\n### 1. 📸 100% Authentic Photos of Famous Places\\nAll placeholder images have been replaced with real, verified, high-resolution photographs from Wikimedia Commons:\\n- **Hundru Falls**: Real 98m cascade dropping on basalt rocks in Ranchi.\\n- **Patratu Valley & Dam**: Authentic twilight view of the winding 30 hairpin ribbon roads and reservoir.\\n- **Baba Baidyanath Dham**: Genuine view of the 72-foot stone spire with rare Panchasula in Deoghar.\\n- **Parasnath Hill (Shikharji)**: Actual panoramic vista of the Anantnatha Tonk along the sacred ridge.\\n- **Betla National Park**: Entrance gate and Sal forest landscape.\\n- **Dassam Falls**: Real photography of the Kanchi river cascade.\\n- **Jonha Falls (Gautamdhara)**: True hanging valley waterfall.\\n- **Netarhat**: The pine plantations and mist of the Queen of Chotanagpur.\\n- **Lodh Falls (Burha Ghaag)**: 143-meter multi-tiered giant in Latehar.\\n- **Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary**: Hilltop elephant sanctuary overlook.\\n- **Tagore Hill (Morabadi)**: Shanti Dham stone pavilion atop the granite hill.\\n- **Maithon Dam & Lake**: The blue water reservoir and green islands.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. 🎒 The MAD \\\"Tourist Explorer Passport\\\" Unlock Experience\\nThe website now functions like an 